Subject: Add a per-site polymorphic property cache to a compiled function

What this does
  Gives JSFunctionBytecode a table of four (shape, offset, kind) entries per
  property site, filled from compiled code by qjs_aot_poly_fill.

Why we need it
  A property site the profile saw with 2-4 shapes cannot use the single
  shape cell a monomorphic site uses, so it exited every time.

What it adds
  JSAotPolyEntry, JSFunctionBytecode.aot_poly/.aot_poly_sites
  qjs_aot_poly_fill(ctx, f, site, obj, atom, write, *off)
  js_aot_poly_free_all, called before the final collection
  JSAotGenLayout.off_fnbc_aot_poly, .off_fnbc_aot_poly_sites, .aot_poly_ways

The table is allocated when the function binds to its compiled entry, so
filling a site from compiled code never allocates: an allocation there
would be a safepoint mid-instruction, and the compiled frame is not
prepared for one. For the same reason the fill refuses an unhashed shape
instead of hashing it: hashing can resize the runtime's shape table, and
an unhashed shape can be mutated in place under the cached offset.

Bytecode version
  No.

